# RIDENOVA — SCHEDULED ADVANCE RIDE BOOKING SYSTEM
## Complete Production-Ready Master Implementation Prompt

### PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Implement a complete, production-oriented Scheduled Advance Booking system in my existing RideNova application. This must be a real, fully connected feature across the customer frontend, driver frontend, admin dashboard, backend APIs, PostgreSQL/Supabase database, payment gateway, notifications, scheduling engine, and ride lifecycle.

This is not a design-only task. Do not merely add a new card, modal, mock data, buttons, endpoints, or backend functions that are not connected to the actual frontend. Implement the complete end-to-end workflow, including the UI/UX, database persistence, server-side authorization, payment verification, driver assignment, notifications, scheduled execution, cancellation rules, and final payment reconciliation.

The existing application supports immediate/live ride bookings. Preserve that working functionality and introduce scheduled bookings as a separate, properly integrated booking mode.

The final experience must look premium, consistent, trustworthy, responsive, and suitable for a real ride-booking platform.

