# SECTION L — CANCELLATION, REASSIGNMENT, AND REFUNDS

## L1. Customer Cancellation

Provide a visible cancellation action in the scheduled booking details whenever cancellation is allowed.

Before confirming cancellation, show:

- The booking status.
- Whether the cancellation is permitted.
- Any applicable cancellation fee.
- The expected refund amount.
- The expected refund method and status.
- Any applicable non-refundable fees.

Use a confirmation dialog so the customer does not cancel accidentally.

The backend must recheck cancellation eligibility when processing the request.

Prevent cancellation of a completed booking. Apply the configured policy for bookings that are already in progress or near pickup.

## L2. Driver Cancellation

Allow driver cancellation or withdrawal only according to the existing driver-discretion and operational policies.

Record a cancellation reason and timestamp.

Notify the customer and admin. Reopen driver assignment if the booking is still valid and enough time remains before pickup.

Do not allow a driver to cancel a booking and leave the customer’s interface stuck on “Driver assigned.”

Prevent duplicate assignments during reassignment.

## L3. Refund Rules

Create a configurable refund policy that authorised administrators can adjust.

Refund decisions should depend on booking state, cancellation timing, applicable fees, and whether the platform or customer initiated cancellation.

Use the payment provider’s real refund API where supported.

Track refund requests and provider references. Update the status only after verified provider responses or webhooks.

Support refund pending, refund failed, partially refunded, and fully refunded states as appropriate.

Do not delete a payment record after a refund. Preserve the complete payment and refund audit trail.

Never claim that money has been refunded merely because a refund request was created.

